        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>IdleZomb — Create. Sacrifice. Evolve.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to <i>IdleZomb</i>, a management game where the twist is… your NPCs are zombies.<br>No villagers to protect here you build, optimize, and experiment using the undead.<br>Sacrificed in the name of progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a ruined world, you take control of an abandoned hospital — the starting point for a potential new species…<br>One that might be more evolved than the one that destroyed everything.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Start with a single zombie</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every game begins with a single randomly generated zombie.<br>Its stats will determine its value… and its chances of survival.<br>Put it to work: harvesting, producing, upgrading…<br>Or sacrifice it to extract precious strands of DNA.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Rebuild your base</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your hospital is the heart of the system. It's where new zombies are born.<br>Nearby, a rundown lab houses a strange figure — one who can butcher your zombies to harvest their DNA.<br>But… are you sure he has good intentions?<br>That’s a question worth remembering.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Content up to level 60</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Currently, each zombie can evolve up to <strong>level 125.</strong> Content is available up to level 60. Each level up requires DNA and improves your stats.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the current update, your zombies will be <strong>able to upgrade</strong> at level 20, 40: new sprite, stat multiplier, and a more prominent presence in this arid desert.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Unexpected events &amp; new gameplay loops</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This update introduces a new gameplay loop centered around unexpected events, bringing resources, collectibles, and added variety to progression.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One event is currently available</strong>, with five more planned to expand the system in future updates.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A world to rebuild… one chicken at a time</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At first, your zombies will only face chickens — harmless and barely nourishing.<br>With time, they’ll encounter mutant rats tougher foes...<br>And far worse creatures in future updates.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>An Early Access in progress</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>IdleZomb</i> is under active development.<br>This early beta is just the first slice of the project.<br>More content, new creatures, gameplay systems, and building types are planned for the coming months.<br>Your feedback is essential.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>An experimental version</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⚠️ This version is not representative of the final game.<br>Many systems are still in development, sounds are not yet integrated,<br>and some elements like the tutorial may contain display bugs.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>IdleZomb — Create. Sacrifice. Evolve.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to <i>IdleZomb</i>, a management game where the twist is… your NPCs are zombies.<br>No villagers to protect here you build, optimize, and experiment using the undead.<br>Sacrificed in the name of progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In a ruined world, you take control of an abandoned hospital — the starting point for a potential new species…<br>One that might be more evolved than the one that destroyed everything.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Start with a single zombie</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every game begins with a single randomly generated zombie.<br>Its stats will determine its value… and its chances of survival.<br>Put it to work: harvesting, producing, upgrading…<br>Or sacrifice it to extract precious strands of DNA.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Rebuild your base</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your hospital is the heart of the system. It's where new zombies are born.<br>Nearby, a rundown lab houses a strange figure — one who can butcher your zombies to harvest their DNA.<br>But… are you sure he has good intentions?<br>That’s a question worth remembering.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Content up to level 60</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Currently, each zombie can evolve up to <strong>level 125.</strong> Content is available up to level 60. Each level up requires DNA and improves your stats.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In the current update, your zombies will be <strong>able to upgrade</strong> at level 20, 40: new sprite, stat multiplier, and a more prominent presence in this arid desert.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Unexpected events &amp; new gameplay loops</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This update introduces a new gameplay loop centered around unexpected events, bringing resources, collectibles, and added variety to progression.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One event is currently available</strong>, with five more planned to expand the system in future updates.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A world to rebuild… one chicken at a time</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At first, your zombies will only face chickens — harmless and barely nourishing.<br>With time, they’ll encounter mutant rats tougher foes...<br>And far worse creatures in future updates.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>An Early Access in progress</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>IdleZomb</i> is under active development.<br>This early beta is just the first slice of the project.<br>More content, new creatures, gameplay systems, and building types are planned for the coming months.<br>Your feedback is essential.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>An experimental version</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⚠️ This version is not representative of the final game.<br>Many systems are still in development, sounds are not yet integrated,<br>and some elements like the tutorial may contain display bugs.</p>",
